everywhere:
In schemes of ... ‘Here we’ll go,’ and ‘There we’ll stay,’
And ‘Everywhere we’ll prosper in our love,’
Was scarce my business. Let them order it;

everybody's:
Since I have had my tea;
P’raps everybody’s gone away
And just forgotten me.

evermore:
Two and two my guards behind, two and two before,
Two and two on either hand, they guard me evermore;
Me, poor dove, that must not coo--eagle that must not soar.

To lose them from her treasured store;
So shalt thou live for evermore--
Though far thy form from mortal ken--

For her the cool-tongued, her the tranquil-hearted,
Whom evermore I follow wistfully,
Wandering Heaven and Earth and Hell and the four seasons through;

evergreen:
Draw close the curtains
Of branched evergreen;
Change cannot touch them

evening's:
And bustle gaily down;
In evening's cool, you'd spray the lawn
When you came back from town.

evergreens:
The pillow of this daring head
Is pungent evergreens;
His larder -- terse and militant --

eves:
Morns that pass by,
Fair eves that fly;
Come buy, come buy:

Yet, a branch, He prunes for fruit;
Yet, a sheep, these eves and morns,
He seeks for me among the thorns.
